{{define "content"}}<h1>You've been invited.</h1>
<p>A place in the Hasala beta is saved for {{.Email}} until {{.Until}}. Open this email on your iPhone.</p>
<p class="code">Your invite code<br><strong>{{if eq (len .Code) 29}}<span class="nw">{{slice .Code 0 15}}</span><wbr><span class="nw">{{slice .Code 15}}</span>{{else}}{{.Code}}{{end}}</strong><br>Saved until {{.Until}}</p>
<ol>
<li><a href="https://hasala.app/testflight">Get TestFlight</a>, Apple's free app for betas, on your iPhone.</li>
{{if .ManualTestFlight}}<li>Accept Apple's invitation and install Hasala. We'll add you to Hasala's TestFlight beta ourselves, and Apple then emails you the invitation: open it on your iPhone, tap View in TestFlight, then Accept and Install.</li>{{else}}<li>Accept Apple's invitation and install Hasala. Apple emails you the invitation separately, and it can arrive before or after this email: open it on your iPhone, tap View in TestFlight, then Accept and Install. You don't need an App Store Connect account, and other testers can't see you.</li>{{end}}
<li>Open Hasala and paste or type your invite, or tap the button below. You'll set up sign-in and write down 12 words.</li>
</ol>
<p><a class="button" href="{{.InviteURL}}">Open my invite</a></p>
<p>Button not working? Open {{.FallbackText}} on your iPhone, or type the code in the app.</p>
<p>Invites are personal and work once, with {{.Email}} only. Not expecting this? You can ignore it.</p>
{{if .LeaveURL}}<p>Changed your mind? <a href="{{.LeaveURL}}">Leave the list</a></p>{{end}}{{end}}
